A platform is forming around what we leave on the table. Right now a conversation keeps the move we made. Pantheon could also keep the strongest move we could have made, why it mattered, and when it might be worth picking up again.

Take “Checking platforms.” The branch we played was about moving from a public thread to a private call. The branch we recovered was about switching from explaining an escape to looking for one in the conversation we were having. And there’s a third branch still on the table. We could give that same exchange to a fresh reader and see what opening they find. What they come up with could be worth keeping even if it was never what you meant.

Now imagine that as social media. A post forks at the line where somebody sees a different possibility. One person writes the next scene. Another tries the idea in their own life and brings back what happened. The original author can pick up a branch they never would’ve written. The social action is “here’s what I made from this.” A like tells you something landed. A fork lets you see where it went.

That’s a platform Pantheon is already starting to sketch. Silent Guitar finds the opening, Dragonfly makes another route visible, opportunity cost tells us which route is worth our time, and the repo gives us a place to return to it. The smallest version is one original line, the reply it got, and one alternate continuation worth playing. We already have the first one.